  "term": "chloral hydrate",
  "definition": "Chloral hydrate is a synthetic drug that depresses activity in the central nervous system, giving it sedative, sleep-inducing, and anticonvulsant effects. In the body it is converted to trichloroethanol and acts on several neurotransmitter-related ion channels, including increasing GABA-A receptor activity.",
